<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ali ibn Yusuf</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. <a href="/years/1106">1106</a>–<a href="/years/1143">1143</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almoravid-empire">Almoravid Empire</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ali ibn Yusuf was the Almoravid ruler from 1106 to 1143, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yusuf-ibn-tashfin">Yusuf ibn Tashfin</a>. He presided over the empire at its greatest extent, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-andalus">al-Andalus</a>, and supported building and religious scholarship. His reign also saw growing Christian pressure in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberia">Iberia</a> and the rise of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almohad-caliphate">Almohad</a> movement, which began the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almoravid-empire">Almoravids</a>' decline.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ali-ibn-yusuf.jpg" alt="Ali ibn Yusuf" width="320" height="155" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: LouisAragon (uploader) · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coin_of_Almoravid_ruler_Ali_ibn_Yusuf,_struck_at_the_Isbiliya_(Seville)_mint.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Under <b>Ali ibn Yusuf</b> (r. 1106–1143), Andalusian culture flowed across the Strait into Marrakesh: Andalusian secretaries, artists and architects transformed the capital, introducing urban institutions, architectural refinement and intellectual culture far removed from the desert tradition from which the dynasty had sprung.</blockquote><a href="/empire/almoravid-empire">Almoravid Empire · Socioeconomy</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Ceuta under Muslim rule, in what is now <a href="/countries/morocco">Morocco</a>. Died in Marrakech, in what is now <a href="/countries/morocco">Morocco</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=35.89,-5.31&amp;year=1124" aria-label="Ceuta under Muslim rule on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4416 868 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Ali ibn Yusuf"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4866 1138h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4866 1138h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=35.89,-5.31&amp;year=1124">What was here in 1124? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
